description:
FILED s473t4 (#1501 CHECK 1 round 1, 2026-09-13).  t/op/lvref.t is TRANSPILE-FAIL: P 199/2, C 0/0 -- the whole file, 201 rows.

    $ ./pl2cl < t/op/lvref.t
    Parser2 TODO: non-scalar state declaration outside a named-sub statement: @a

MINIMAL REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):
    use strict; use warnings;
    use feature 'refaliasing', 'state';
    no warnings 'experimental::refaliasing';
    sub f {
      \state @a = [1..3];
      print "@a\n";
    }
    f(); f();
    perl: "1 2 3" twice
    pcl : Transpile failed: Parser2 TODO: non-scalar state declaration outside
          a named-sub statement: @a

THE SITE in the file is t/op/lvref.t:313-321 (`\state @a = [1..3]`, `\state @c = [$_]`, `\state %y = {1,2}`), i.e. the refaliasing-a-state-container family.

MECHANISM: Pl/Parser2.pm's state handler requires the declaring STATEMENT to be a PPI::Statement::Variable whose parent is a Block or the Document.  In `\state @a = ...` the `state` word sits inside a Cast-led expression statement, so the walk that looks for the enclosing named sub never starts and the container path dies.  The scalar spelling `\state $x = \$y` should be probed in the same pass -- it may take the same route.

RELATED: #1332 / the refaliasing family (grep DECIDED for "refaliasing"); the s396 round shipped the parenthesised-array spellings and filed #332 for the ones it did not.  This is an unshipped spelling of the same family, not a new mechanism -- but it is a term-grammar change, so it is round t5a work, not a filler.
